## The Pattern: Scoped Service + Interactive Islands

The core challenge: **static SSR components cannot reactively re-render**. Your MainLayout is static, so it renders once per navigation. The solution is:

1. **A scoped `ThemeService`** — `AddScoped` gives per-circuit isolation in Blazor Server.
2. **Embed interactive islands** in the static layout for anything that must react to changes (e.g., `<ThemeIndicator @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />`).
3. All interactive components subscribe to the service's `OnChanged` event.

### Architecture

```
┌─ MainLayout (Static SSR) ─────────────────────────┐
│  ┌─ ThemeIndicator (@rendermode InteractiveServer)─┐│
│  │  Subscribes to ThemeService.OnChanged           ││
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘│
│  @Body (per-page interactive)                       │
│    └─ SettingsPanel subscribes to ThemeService      │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Key pieces:

**ThemeService.cs** — registered as `builder.Services.AddScoped<ThemeService>()`
```csharp
public class ThemeService
{
    public Theme CurrentTheme { get; private set; } = Theme.System;
    public string AccentColor { get; private set; } = "#0078d4";

    public event Action? OnChanged;

    public void SetTheme(Theme theme)
    {
        CurrentTheme = theme;
        OnChanged?.Invoke();
    }

    public void SetAccentColor(string color)
    {
        AccentColor = color;
        OnChanged?.Invoke();
    }
}

public enum Theme { Light, Dark, System }
```

**ThemeIndicator.razor** — placed in layout with `@rendermode InteractiveServer`
```razor
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@inject ThemeService Theme
@implements IDisposable

<span class="theme-badge" style="color: @Theme.AccentColor">
    @Theme.CurrentTheme
</span>

@code {
    protected override void OnInitialized() => Theme.OnChanged += StateHasChanged;
    public void Dispose() => Theme.OnChanged -= StateHasChanged;
}
```

**In MainLayout.razor** (stays static):
```razor
<header>
    <ThemeIndicator />  @* ← interactive island in static layout *@
</header>
<article>@Body</article>
```

### Why this works for all 5 requirements:

| # | Requirement | How |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Read/write from anywhere | Inject `ThemeService` in any component |
| 2 | Immediate cross-component updates | `OnChanged` event → `StateHasChanged` |
| 3 | Settings page updates header | Same scoped instance, same event |
| 4 | Per-user isolation | `AddScoped` = per-circuit in Server mode |
| 5 | Persists across enhanced nav | Circuit (and its scoped services) survives enhanced navigation |

The critical insight: **you can't make the layout itself reactive, but you can plant interactive components inside it** that share the same DI scope as your page components.
